WEBVTT

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.310
Pocket Monsters...

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.250
Pokémon for short.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:23.090
The strange, strange creatures
who live on this planet.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.860
In the forests,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.340
in the skies,

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.510
in the seas,

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.600
and in space...

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.320
You can find them
all over the world.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:04.210
And... One Pokémon is said to hold
the genes of all Pokémon...

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:05.140
Mew!

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:14.370
As a matter of fact, psychic energy
thought to belong to Mew has been detected.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.170
What?!

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.270
This is the Sakuragi Institute,
which researches Pokémon.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.800
Mew is...

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.340
Does that mean Mew’s there?

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:30.530
It’s not impossible.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.620
Hear that? What now, Go?

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:37.700
I... might get to catch Mew!

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.830
These boys are Satoshi and Go.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:46.040
As research fellows,
or special lab assistants,

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.490
they have met and
interacted with Pokémon,

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:50.780
sharing many
different experiences.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:55.030
Director Sakuragi!
I wanna go see Mew!

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.880
I’ll go, I’ll go!
I’ll go for sure!

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.930
I thought you’d say that,
so I arranged for a boat.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.440
Yay!

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.940
That’s great!

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:07.070
Ever since they first met
at the Pokémon Camp,

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:09.190
Mew has been Go’s inspiration.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.740
More than my inspiration,
it’s my target, yeah?

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.770
Huh?
Koharu, what about school?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.470
See you later!

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.740
So, where is it?

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.030
Where’s Mew?

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.130
Right. As for that... Kikuna?

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:33.090
There was only one landmass in the area
where the psychic energy was detected.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.600
Here, the isolated isle of Cello Island!

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.810
An isle surrounded by steep cliffs
that keep people away. It’s very mysterious!

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.750
That gets me fired up!

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:45.770
Yeah!

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.440
To understand Pokémon is
to understand the world.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.920
As a researcher myself,
I pray that you do get to see Mew.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:55.820
Yeah!

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.210
This is Cello Island...?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.820
Mew is somewhere
on this island!

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.050
Satoshi!

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:06.920
Yeah!

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.300
Let’s go!

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.740
All right!
Where should we start?

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.500
Ta-daah!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:14.880
We’re close enough that my special sensor
can pick up Mew’s psychic energy...

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.290
Huh? Nothing detected...

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.540
Then let’s just look wherever.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.680
In this huge jungle?!

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.390
I’m going first!

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:24.850
Wait for me!

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.040
Poppo! Onisuzume!

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.860
Butterfree, too!

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.160
A Mankey!

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.750
Monster Ball, go!

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:02.480
Mankey’s data will be
added to the index!

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.930
All right!
My first catch of the day!

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.110
Great!

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.910
Huh? Why’d the Mankey stop?

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.120
Go!

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.770
A sinking bog!

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:39.350
Hold on, Satoshi! Go!

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:42.980
Heracross,
I’m counting on you!

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.790
Heracross, catch!

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.360
You saved me, Heracross...

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.500
Water Gun!

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.530
Oh! All cleaned up.

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:06.240
Thanks, Messon.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:09.680
Now, then...

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:12.040
How do we get across...?

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.930
Don’t worry, it’ll work out!

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:17.050
You’re always
so easygoing, Satoshi.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.790
Caterpie, I’m counting on you!

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:32.010
Caterpie, String Shot!

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.640
Okay! Good work!

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.470
I’ll wrap the string here
on a branch...

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.790
And the Caterpie Tightrope
is complete!

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:48.570
Ooh!

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.490
I’ll go first, then!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.390
Sure!

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.900
Pikachu, you hold on tight!

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.380
One, two...

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.500
Okay then, me too...

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:08.840
Kingler?!

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:15.140
Go!

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.560
Go, Monster Ball!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.730
Great!

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.280
All right!

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.600
Go, watch out!

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.580
Well done!

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:37.790
Crab’s data will be
added to the index!

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.500
Successful landing!

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.150
Excellent!

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:46.920
Even when you stumble,
you land feet first, Go.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:52.430
I didn’t <i>stumble.</i> That near-<i>fall</i> was
well within my expectations, yeah!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.440
Let’s cross here.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:56.180
Okay!

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:00.390
Come on, Go!

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.350
I know!

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:07.820
Gyarados?!

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:11.070
Satoshi!

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:13.110
I’m fine!

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.490
Monster Ball, go!

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.670
Pikachu, Electroweb!

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.270
Thanks, Satoshi!

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:39.320
Go! Cross over while you can!

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:40.100
Right!

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.540
Pikachu!

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.700
Lend us a hand, Dewgong!

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.310
Satoshi!

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.880
You’re kidding...

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.890
Dewgong, do your best!

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.500
Pikachu!

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.610
Dewgong, return!

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.320
Pikachu!

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:57.510
Where are we?

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:02.430
We went over the waterfall,
then blacked out...

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:12.940
So cute!

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:15.740
What happened?

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:23.660
Hey, you guys!
Do you live...

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:26.340
They ran off.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.060
Did we frighten them?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.470
Why have you come here?

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.350
Why have you come here?

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:25.120
It talks...?!

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:28.940
No, is this what’s
called telepathy...?

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:30.830
Mewtwo.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.400
Mew... two?

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.200
Did you save us?

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:41.690
Thank you!

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.660
Not Mew, but Mewtwo...

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.210
It is bigger than Mew, I guess.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:50.610
But it gives off kind of
a similar vibe.

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:56.210
I’m getting a reaction!

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.830
What’s going on?!

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:01.530
Or... is Mew
somewhere nearby?!

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.720
You seek Mew?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.600
Yeah!

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.720
To what end?

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.640
I’ll catch it!

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.730
Catching every Pokémon
to reach Mew is my dream!

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.240
Hmm...

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:19.610
How will catching every Pokémon
mean reaching Mew?

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:24.120
To catch a Pokémon is to understand it,
that’s what I believe.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:29.140
I want to catch all sorts of Pokémon,
and learn more about Pokémon!

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:32.290
If I understand every Pokémon,

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:36.640
I can reach Mew,
who holds the genes of every Pokémon!

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:38.190
Go...

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.220
Mewtwo...
You’re a Pokémon, right?

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:52.730
Which means...
I can catch you in a Monster Ball, right?

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:54.920
Catch Mewtwo?!

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:59.070
I want to learn more about you!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:02.190
So... I’ll catch you!

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.370
I am strong.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:08.580
I was created to be
the world’s strongest Pokémon.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.700
Mewtwo!
I want to battle you!

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.610
I wanna beat the strongest
Pokémon in a battle,

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:18.560
to get closer to my dream of
being a Pokémon Master!

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.530
So, you’re fine with that, right?

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:23.470
C’mon, Mewtwo!

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:32.470
As you wish.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:38.230
Then... Put those “dreams” of yours
on the line, and face me!

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:40.940
Let’s go, Pikachu!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.490
Come on out, Aceburn!

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.370
Iron Tail!

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:49.490
Blaze Kick!

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:02.870
Are you okay, Pikachu?

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:07.410
Aceburn!

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:14.130
Satoshi!

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:16.230
Yeah. Combination!

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:18.690
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:24.450
Blaze Kick!

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:29.910
100,000 Volts!

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:38.830
Pikachu!

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:54.650
Rest up here.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.810
Lucario, I choose you!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.750
Aceburn, use Pyro Ball!

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.570
Lucario! Aura Sphere!

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:22.880
Lucario!
Aceburn!

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:27.170
All right!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.130
Good going!

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:30.830
Shadow Clones!

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:32.340
Lightning Speed!

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:39.770
Force Palm!

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:49.610
Don’t give up! Blaze Kick!

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:51.280
Reversal!

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:04.140
Lucario!
Aceburn!

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:08.070
Gah...!

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:13.890
Are you finished?

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:15.260
Not yet!

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.690
Lucario, can you keep going?

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:22.710
Do all you can, Aceburn!

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:27.610
Okay! Shadow Clones!

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:29.230
Pyro Ball!

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:34.730
Aura Sphere!

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.500
Go!

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:53.200
You spoke of your dreams before.

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:57.970
The world is vast.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:01.900
There exist many Pokémon
you cannot even imagine.

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:05.330
Knowing that, will you still
chase your dreams?

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:06.580
Of course!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.500
Always!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.510
Because I have my friends!

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:18.470
It seems you have
formed bonds properly.

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:28.130
Here, here...

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:31.480
However,
not everyone does the same.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:37.660
Do you mean that when
they were scared of us,

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:40.240
it’s because they’d
been hurt by humans?

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:46.500
I get it. Mewtwo rescues
Pokémon like that from people...

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:50.720
This is not a place
for humans to tread.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:55.050
However, I have enjoyed today
more than anything in a long time.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:05.460
Mewtwo!

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.980
Hold on!

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:11.270
You are frail, fleeting, immature...

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:18.990
But that is exactly why
you possess infinite potential...

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:21.370
Mewtwo!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:29.070
Your journey...
has only just begun.

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:42.910
Mewtwo...
was really strong.

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:46.410
Yeah. We’ve still got
a long way to go.

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:49.310
Huh?

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.910
This is the Sakuragi Institute.

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.530
Did Mewtwo bring us here?

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.940
I hope we’ll see it again.

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:05.680
‘Course we will!

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:08.530
After all,
the future lies in my hands!

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.510
<i>Our</i> hands, right?

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:16.460
Go? Satoshi?

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:18.210
Koharu!

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.340
We’re back!

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:20.390
Welcome back!

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:21.920
<i>Welcome back!</i>

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:23.910
How was it?

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:25.350
Did you get to see Mew?

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:32.840
Satoshi and Go will keep running
towards their dreams.

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:38.260
Now then, everyone... A world of dreams and
adventures with Pocket Monsters awaits!

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:39.740
Let’s go!

00:23:07.220 --> 00:23:09.630
Now, onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:13.710
The Pokémon Eating Contest?

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:15.130
That sounds fun!

00:23:15.130 --> 00:23:15.920
Let’s enter, Go!

00:23:15.920 --> 00:23:21.300
How naïve. Kuchiba City’s Eating Contest
is famous for attracting fierce competition.

00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:23.570
If the two favorites face off...

00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:25.570
Then even the winner’s
not getting off lightly.

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:28.000
Team Rocket’s gonna be headed...

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:29.430
straight for the victory road!

00:23:29.430 --> 00:23:31.460
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.460 --> 00:23:34.880
Pokémon Champion!
The Battle of Big Eaters!
